  "description": "QANLOK crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C72 H74 Dy4 N6 O20,2(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.488-3.944 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.09-111.87°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C76H78N8O20Dy4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
